The question was:

> 
> Dear list participants!
> 
> Is there a possibility using the pmvnorm function (bivariate cumulative 
> probability) with the upper right probability P(X > q[1], Y > q[2]) instead 
> of 
the 
> default lower left probability P(X < q[1], Y < q[2])?
> 
> Best thanks in advance,
> Hubert Holzmann. 

The solution is:

Yes, try using:

1 - pnorm(q[1]) - pnorm(q[2]) + pmvnorm(q[1],q[2])

You can put in other mean vectors and VCV matrices, too, as long as you
use the correct marginals in the pnorm functions.

