More flexibility in import options would be appreciated in more than
just Excel.  The ability to force all imported data to be "character"
(and not made into factors) would be a step in the right direction. Even
on comma delimited text files I occasionally run into problems where
someone has coded responses with both alphas and numbers. If a number
happens to be in the first column then all the alphas get made NA. If an
alpha is first, the column gets imported as character and all the data
is present.  The ability to force a character read is present (in the
format string capability in the text input dialog) but very clumsy when
you are importing a large number of variables.

If we were all in full control of the data before we get it many of
these problems could be avoided, but , since we are not, flexibility is
critical.

